<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Piset</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>piset &lt;item&gt; title &lt;text&gt;
piset &lt;item&gt; shortdescr &lt;text&gt;
piset &lt;item&gt; descr
</pre>
<p>Gives one of your power items (see <a cmd='#'>Help Power Items</a>) a look of your 
own. Each can be set once per item, so take your time:
</p>
<ul><li><b>title</b>: what you see when you carry it or wear it (Jewel</li></ul>
<p>Encrusted Anklet).
</p>
<ul><li><b>shortdescr</b>: what you see when it lies on the ground (An anklet</li></ul>
<p>encrusted with fine jewels lies here.).
</p>
<ul><li><b>descr</b>: what you see when you look at it. You write it in the</li></ul>
<p>editor and end it with @ on a line of its own.
</p><p>Before it is set, you are asked whether it is what you want: Y for yes, 
N to type it again, Q to give up. The item must be in your inventory. 
Some unique power items can't be renamed.
</p><p>Keep it fitting for a fantasy world and not offensive: the gods may 
take an item back if it isn't.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Power Items</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Pibag</a>
</pre>




</div>